From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 13:09:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(players): align retained remote spawn origins

AddPlayer supplies feet while MovePlayer supplies an eye position. Initialize the live transform through setJavaPosition so picking proxies and relative clicks align with visible feet from the first frame. Keep Java spawn coordinates at the supplied feet.

Keep the absolute/delta actor receive cache independent from that live spawn transform. Current Bedrock 1.26.60.5/BDS 1.26.60.6 protocol 2225 controls leave fresh player sparse coordinates and angles at zero. A normal MovePlayer does not populate that cache; an actor absolute update does. Preserve constructor flags and duration while initializing the fresh player cache.

Native and pre-fix direct journals carry identical peer payloads. Sparse Z-only updates hide the native fresh player while Java incorrectly retains its spawn height. A separate native control supplies Y/Z with X omitted, then X alone: the player starts at the zero-X projection and returns to center only after explicit X. Fresh replacement peers repeat the result. Absolute/normal/delta mixtures retain the separate actor cache.

The registered regression decodes Java spawn, normal movement and sparse movement. It preserves visible feet and the retained eye origin, and rejects spawn or normal movement leaking into omitted sparse axes and angles. Its fixture uses an empty held-item codec without relying on deferred inventory APIs.

Earlier native upper-body attack controls establish initial picking and outgoing attack admission before and after stationary updates. Their synthetic peers do not establish server damage. Full movement trajectories, arbitrary actors, mounts and complete rendering parity remain unverified.
